Buoys $A$, $B$ and $C$ mark a triangular sailing course. Find the acute angle $\theta=\angle ABC$, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.1394,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.2,2.07846);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$8\text{ km}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$12\text{ km}$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=6mm,angle eccentricity=1.5,"$60^{\circ}$"] {angle=B--A--C};
\pic[draw,angle radius=7mm,angle eccentricity=1.5,"$\theta$"] {angle=C--B--A};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A leaning brace forms triangle $ABC$. Given that $\theta=\angle ACB$ is obtuse, find $\theta$, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.8,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.76697,1.02016);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$12\text{ m}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=7mm,angle eccentricity=1.5,"$30^{\circ}$"] {angle=B--A--C};
\pic[draw,angle radius=4mm,angle eccentricity=1.6,"$\theta$"] {angle=A--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
